"about": "A small book in two parts, light enough to carry to the museum. Each opening is one century, a ruled page for writing facing a plain page for drawing, as in the interleaved books the P.U.S. children kept from 1914. The centuries run, as in Mrs. Epps’s museum note-book, from the forty-fifth before Christ to our own; the first part ends at the birth of Christ and the second begins there.",
"how": [
"Print each booklet on A4, on both sides, turning on the short edge.",
"Keep the sheets in order, fold them in half together, and staple twice along the fold. Each makes an A5 book.",
"Take whichever part you need on the day."
],
