"title": "Year 2: on to card and a craft knife",
"forWho": "Read with Mum before the first model.",
"text": [
[
"What changes",
"From Year 2, Happy Handicrafts moves on to thicker paper (good cardstock or Bristol board), a craft knife and a cutting mat. Joanna: “These obviously require parental oversight.”"
],
[
"Cardboard sloyd",
"Joanna explains that cardboard sloyd is the next step after paper sloyd, and that Charlotte Mason called sloyd “the most valuable and most educative of all the handicrafts”. Little by little, children learn to cut with the knife along a line by eye, without a ruler."
],
[
"Do every model",
"Each model builds on the skills of the one before, so don’t skip one just because you have no use for it. Practise each over several weeks until it can be made confidently and alone, but stop before it stops being enjoyable."
]
],
