"intro": "A step at a time, following the order the schools of Charlotte Mason’s day used (needle drill, hemming, seaming, felling, then something useful), with the PNEU’s set book, The Little Girl’s Sewing Book.",
"source": "Schedule III (Needlework) of the Education Code, printed in the appendix of Amy K. Smith, Needlework for Student Teachers (1897).",
