"forWho": "Both girls",
"steps": [
"Keep the paint box and palette clean, and the water clean; use a separate brush to bring water to the palette.",
"Once colour is on the paper, don’t touch it again while it is wet.",
"Flat graded wash: start at the top with a full brush, guide the floating colour down the page, taking more water and less colour as you go.",
"Lay one colour beside another so they run together while wet.",
"Make a secondary colour by passing one colour over another when the first is dry, e.g. blue over pink for violet."
],
"src": "Mrs. H. Perrin, “Brush Drawing”, Parents’ Review vol. 4 (1893/94), pp. 344–346 and 453–457, after Ebenezer Cooke (AmblesideOnline)."
